[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Night Vision - Configurable[/color][/b][/size]

See in the dark with a [b]neutral white-light radius[/b], [b]Fullscreen[/b] brightness, or [b]Natural[/b] vision: a bright central oval fading into the darkness around the screen. Add a softly fading vampire vignette, black-and-white shading or red tint in [b]5% steps[/b].

Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/294]Night Vision by opogode[/url], [b]made with permission[/b].

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Controls[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Keyboard:[/color][/b] Press N to toggle night vision in vampire form.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Controller:[/color][/b] Hold L3 / the left stick for 0.6 seconds. Release between toggles.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Stays on until you turn it off[/color][/b][/size]

Once enabled, vision stays on until you toggle it off or return to human form. Loading a save or switching player or camera preserves your choice and automatically resumes the effect when ready. A new game session starts with vision off. A brief brightness pulse marks Fullscreen activation.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Open [b]Mod Settings > Night Vision - Configurable[/b]. Press Apply to save changes and adjust active vision immediately.

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Enabled:[/color][/b] Enables the mod; switching it Off also turns vision off. Enabling it again does not activate vision automatically. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Night Vision Mode:[/color][/b] Radius casts soft light centered on your character, with a broad, gradual fade and reduced shiny highlights. Fullscreen brightens the whole view. Natural brightens a broad central oval, including distant scenery, with normal darkness at the edges and no activation flash. Use Natural with SDR output. Default: Natural. Existing saved mode choices are preserved.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Natural size:[/color][/b] Outer oval size from 40–100% in 5% steps. Shown only in Natural mode. Default: 90%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Fade softness:[/color][/b] Portion of Natural’s radius that fades gradually, from 20–100% in 5% steps. Shown only in Natural mode. Default: 70%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Light radius:[/color][/b] 5–50 metres in 1-metre steps. Shown only in Radius mode. Default: 6 metres.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vignette:[/color][/b] Soft red veins from the game's vampire blood-hunger texture. Hidden in menus; does not trigger hunger or damage effects. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vignette opacity:[/color][/b] 0–100% strength in 5% steps. Shown only with Vignette On. Default: 20%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Black & White:[/color][/b] 0% keeps natural colours; 100% is black and white. Adjustable in 5% steps. Default: 0%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Keep blood red:[/color][/b] Preserve red shades with Black & White, including blood and similarly red objects. The vampire border stays red too. Requires HDR output off. Dark or discoloured blood may lose some colour. Default: Off.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Red brightness:[/color][/b] Shown with Keep blood red On. Brighten preserved world reds from 100–500% in 10% steps. 100% is the original brightness. The border remains separately controlled. Default: 100%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Red tint:[/color][/b] 0–100% in 5% steps. Colours only the added light in Radius mode, or the whole view in Fullscreen mode. Hidden and unused in Natural, retaining its saved value. The border stays red independently. Default: 0%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Brightness:[/color][/b] 25–300% in 5% steps. 100% is normal game brightness in Fullscreen and Natural, or standard light strength in Radius. Natural changes only the central oval. Default: 200%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Controller shortcut:[/color][/b] Enables the left-stick hold. Keyboard N remains available. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Logging:[/color][/b] Writes setup, activation and aggregate diagnostics to ue4ss/UE4SS.log. Default: Off.
[/list]

Without the menu, close the game, edit NightVisionConfigurable/settings.ini after it has been generated on first launch, and restart. The included settings.ini.example lists the defaults.

Menus temporarily hide all vision effects; returning to gameplay restores them without another toggle. Pausing, showing the cursor, blocking movement or hiding gameplay UI also suspends the effects and shortcuts. Turning vision off removes the light and border and restores camera values still owned by the mod. No extra bloom or chromatic aberration is added.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Night-Vision-Configurable.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive’s Dawnwalker folder into The Blood of Dawnwalker’s game folder, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/294]Night Vision by opogode[/url] — made with permission. This independent implementation does not redistribute the original mod's script or assets.

Thanks to the UE4SS contributors and to mmarcussa for Mod Setting Menu and its integration helper. The bundled ue4ss-common settings modules are MIT licensed. Dependency notices are included in the archive.

Banner and thumbnail: official in-game screenshot from the [url=https://rebel-wolves.com/en/press-center]Rebel Wolves press kit[/url], with a crop and title overlay. Illustrative promotional imagery.

